-align:baseline;font-size:24pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous YouTube Engine Research Pass 4A: Research &amp; Intelligence Ecosystem Discovery</span></h1><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Executive Summary</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The primary objective of this discovery pass is to establish a high-reliability Research &amp; Intelligence layer for the autonomous YouTube Content &amp; Video Production Engine, operated under the master direction of Hermes. Rather than engineering custom search engines, web scrapers, or document parsing tools from scratch, this investigation applies a strict capability waterfall to identify, evaluate, and integrate existing, highly maintained open-source software, Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, agent frameworks, and official platform APIs.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The research intelligence ecosystem must support an end-to-end pipeline progressing from research planning and web discovery to source validation, fact extraction, trend tracking, viral outlier detection, competitive analysis, and structured research brief generation. Discovery demonstrates that the broader open-source and API ecosystem provides mature, production-grade solutions for virtually every stage of this pipeline. Autonomous deep research agents such as </span><span style="font-weight:700">GPT Researcher</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">LangChain Open Deep Research</span><span>&nbsp;offer robust planning, recursive searching, and citation-backed synthesis. Dynamic web extraction is efficiently satisfied by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Crawl4AI</span><span>&nbsp;and its standardized skill packages, which generate cleaned, token-optimized Markdown. Document parsing and structured fact ingestion are handled natively by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Docling</span><span>, while search trends can be monitored via </span><span style="font-weight:700">pytrends-modern</span><span>&nbsp;and the official </span><span style="font-weight:700">Google Trends API (Alpha)</span><span>. Platform intelligence relies on optimized requests to the </span><span style="font-weight:700">YouTube Data API v3</span><span>, supplemented by </span><span style="font-weight:700">ClaimBuster</span><span>&nbsp;and the </span><span style="font-weight:700">Google Fact Check Tools API</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;for claim verification.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Custom development is strictly limited to a single algorithmic logic component: channel-relative viral velocity calculation, which can be executed seamlessly as a standard Python analytical task within the Hermes orchestration framework.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Capability Map</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The capability matrix evaluates candidates against system requirements following the mandatory capability waterfall: Hermes Native \rightarrow Hermes Skill \rightarrow Hermes Tool \rightarrow MCP \rightarrow Hermes Plugin \rightarrow API/CLI \rightarrow Existing OSS \rightarrow Free/Local Resource \rightarrow Existing Project Resource \rightarrow Custom Build.</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:42.5pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Research Capability</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:42.5pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padd